===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|cilice|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|cilicium||clothing made of goatskin|lang=la}}, from {{m|en|Cilicia}} where it originates from.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hairshirt]].
# {{context|chiefly|in Opus Dei|lang=en}} A [[leather]] [[strap]] [[stud]]ded with [[metallic]] [[barb]]s that cut into [[flesh]] as a constant [[reminder]] of [[Christ]]'s [[suffering]].

